			<div class="content" id="post-content-2468466">
									

<p>There is a bit of redundancy in the paragraphs that discuss the variations in the duplicates. Namely the bolded parts below:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Multiple such duplicates have appeared for single agents, however <strong>differences (namely in weight, build, tattoo patterns, etc.) have been cited between instances and related persons</strong> (See Addendum 1 for details). Most intact SCP-2446-1 manifest in an early state of putrefaction.</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-2446-1 tend to appear in dress similar to Foundation-issue Mobile Task Force combat gear. <strong>Style and composition of such dress (as well as worn equipment) vary with some frequency.</strong> SCP-2446-1 which do not manifest in MTF gear manifest in standard civilian clothes. <strong>Certain physical factors, like the weight of an instance, vary between duplicates</strong>, however genetic makeup never seriously differs. <strong>Clothes and gear retrieved from SCP-2446-1 also vary in style and construction.</strong></p>
</blockquote>
<p>The last two sentences can pretty much be entirely removed, since they don't add any new information.</p>
<p>Also,</p>
<blockquote>
<p>certain reading fall outside</p>
</blockquote>
<p>should be &quot;readings&quot;.</p>

