<p>I had initially downvoted when this first appeared, based on the fact that it was lacking supplements and that it employed humes<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-927317-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-927317-1')">1</a></sup>. However, with the other material supplied, I could see that this was something that was heavily context-dependent, so I went back to read again with an open mind.</p>
<p>As a concept and as the opening of a larger narrative, this <em>could</em> work. The initial pitch is one that I would say is interesting, and I found myself wanting to know more. Unfortunately, the story that followed didn't quite live up to the initial interest of the premise. As such, my downvote remains. This isn't bad, but it doesn't feel like it quite hit what it was aiming for.</p>
